# Whitelist pattern: ignore everything at the top level, then re-admit only what
# belongs in a PUBLIC repo. Safer than blacklisting, because anything new that
# lands in this folder is excluded until someone deliberately adds it.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/book/

# --- inside book/ -----------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered output is a build artifact, not source. Committing 14 MB binaries on
# every rebuild would bloat history; publish via CI or Releases instead.
/book/render/

# --- deliberately excluded and why ------------------------------------------
# bme-notion-export/    103 MB frozen Notion archive. Superseded by book/content
#                       and kept locally only. It is also a whole-workspace
#                       export, so it contains unrelated personal material.
# *.pdf (top level)     "A Beginner's Guide to mBot" is Makeblock's copyrighted
#                       documentation. Link to it, do not redistribute it.
# mbot_board.jpg        Makeblock product photograph, same reasoning.
# review-basics.md      Internal review notes and working files. See README.
# check-on-robot.md
# manual-edits-in-notion.md
# notion-comments-archive.md
# notion-todo-backlog.md
# info.md

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
